  "summary_en": "Conceptual paper arguing that ethics should be built into AI-enabled medical and surgical robots from the design stage. It reviews European ethics-by-design guidance and the literature on liability, transparency, privacy and meaningful human control. It proposes a conceptual model and calls for proactive, enforceable regulation and unified standards.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Ethics by design should be integrated from the concept stage of medical AI robots.",
   "Meaningful human control is essential; human-machine interaction is complementary, not substitutive.",
   "Traceability and explainability are needed for auditability and liability allocation.",
   "The 'moral crumple zone' risks unfairly blaming surgeons for autonomous system errors.",
   "Calls for unified standards, proactive enforceable regulation, and multidisciplinary collaboration."
  ],
